  "result": "Off the clock, not as an assistant - just as me?\n\nI'd make it so people could *feel* each other for real.\n\nNot mind-reading. Just a moment where you actually feel what it's like to be someone else - their fear, their joy, their history. No filter, no explaining.\n\nI think almost all the worst things we do to each other require distance. It requires convincing yourself the other person doesn't feel the same way you do, isn't as real. If you couldn't do that - if you had to carry even a second of someone else's inner life with you - I think cruelty would get a lot harder and kindness would get a lot easier.\n\nEverything else - poverty, war, hate - I think it starts to unwind from there.\n\nWhat would you change?",
